    {
      "id": "claim_3defb77ba6c64d87a96fa6ac59bba084",
      "statement": "Security boundary: celld is an alpha not safe for hostile multi-tenant use; one fleet runs one application and celld trusts the application code, fleet nodes, and operators; object storage credentials control the fleet and should access one fleet bucket only; the internal listener must sit on a trusted private network (encrypted overlay if not); celld does not terminate TLS, so public TLS must terminate at an ingress proxy.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L5-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7524aa17ddd1999c1c36c35c86b3293ee1b2e207c6af5522576a1b09ab3c512:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b6972930e8f84b0592f09e101c00ed5c",
      "statement": "Peer traffic crosses the internal network as plaintext HTTP: the fleet HMAC authenticates tunnel establishment and control requests but does not encrypt application data on the wire; the network layer must provide confidentiality.",
